      "title": "Who is acting for whom?",
      "narration": "Aisha is a licensed life producer. Marcus asks whether she can promise that every application will be approved. She cannot. A producer's role and authority have limits. In a typical insurer agency relationship, the insurer is the principal and the producer is its agent. The principal authorizes the agent to perform specified acts on its behalf. The producer may have duties to applicants and insureds as well. The word agent identifies a relationship; it does not mean permission to rewrite a policy or ignore underwriting.",
